{"title":"Career Roadmap · Design Manager","role":"Design Manager","summary":"A Design Manager coordinates the design process from initial brief through design development, documentation, coordination, approvals, procurement support, construction, and final delivery.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Interior Architecture & Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Design Manager coordinates the design process from initial brief through design development, documentation, coordination, approvals, procurement support, construction, and final delivery."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Interior Architecture & Design graduate, the role sits between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design","Architecture","Interior Systems","Clients","Consultants","Contractors","Project Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A Design Manager may coordinate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interior architecture"},{"text":"Architectural design"},{"text":"Structural consultants"},{"text":"MEP consultants"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Furniture and finishes"},{"text":"Brand/design standards"},{"text":"BIM teams"},{"text":"Vendors"},{"text":"Contractors"},{"text":"Cost consultants"},{"text":"Project managers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical projects include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate offices"},{"text":"Hospitality"},{"text":"Retail"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Residential developments"},{"text":"Airports"},{"text":"Educational institutions"},{"text":"Commercial buildings"},{"text":"Mixed-use developments"},{"text":"High-end interiors"},{"text":"Workplace environments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The career is therefore broader than simply being an interior designer. The goal is to become the person who can control design quality, coordination, information, timelines, and delivery across multiple disciplines."}]},{"headi